model.en:
Step 1 — Define notification interfaces in the Use Cases ring:
```
interface IEmailNotifier { sendInvoiceGenerated(to: Email, invoiceId: InvoiceId): Promise<void>; }
interface ISmsNotifier  { sendBillingAlert(to: PhoneNumber, message: string): Promise<void>; }
```
These are secondary ports — same pattern as IOrderRepository. They are owned by the Use Cases ring.

Step 2 — Inject into the interactor:
```
class GenerateInvoiceInteractor {
  constructor(
    private readonly emailNotifier: IEmailNotifier,
    private readonly smsNotifier: ISmsNotifier,
    // ... other dependencies
  ) {}
}
```

Step 3 — Implement in the outer ring:
```
// Frameworks/Infrastructure ring
class SendGridEmailAdapter implements IEmailNotifier { ... }
class TwilioSmsAdapter implements ISmsNotifier { ... }
```

Step 4 — Wire in the composition root (Frameworks ring or main):
```
new GenerateInvoiceInteractor(
  new SendGridEmailAdapter(sendgridApiKey),
  new TwilioSmsAdapter(twilioConfig),
  ...
)
```

Result: the interactor calls domain-language methods on interfaces it owns. SendGrid and Twilio are invisible to the inner rings. Swapping to a different email provider requires only a new adapter class in the outer ring.

